@startuml erd-fulfilment
title Entity Relationships — Fulfilment (Draft v1)

entity "shipments" as s {
  * id : bigint <<PK>>
  --
  * cargo_offer_id : bigint <<FK,unique>>
  * carrier_id : bigint <<FK>>
  * shipper_id : bigint <<FK>>
  * vehicle_id : bigint <<FK>>
  * status : string [draft, quoted, accepted, in_transit, delivered, settled, cancelled]
  pickup_at : datetime
  delivered_at : datetime
  settled_at : datetime
  cancelled_at : datetime
  deleted_at : datetime
  * created_at : datetime
  * updated_at : datetime
}

entity "tracking_events" as te {
  * id : bigint <<PK>>
  --
  * shipment_id : bigint <<FK>>
  * event_type : string [quoted, accepted, picked_up, waypoint, position, delay, delivered, settled, cancelled, exception]
  * occurred_at : datetime
  lat : decimal(9,6)
  lng : decimal(9,6)
  note : text
  * created_at : datetime
  * updated_at : datetime
}

entity "routes" as r {
  * id : bigint <<PK>>
  --
  * shipment_id : bigint <<FK,unique>>
  polyline : text
  waypoints_json : text
  eta : datetime
  provider : string [google, here, osrm]
  * created_at : datetime
  * updated_at : datetime
}

s ||--o{ te : "emits"
s ||--o| r : "has planned route"

note bottom
  Soft-delete on shipments (deleted_at; ADR-009). Lat / lng on
  tracking_events stored as DECIMAL(9,6) (ADR-010); no spatial index
  Phase 0/1. FSM transitions documented in
  docs/02-high-level-design/domain-model.md § 4.1.

  Cross-context FK: shipments.vehicle_id → vehicles.id (Identity). The
  vehicle is copied from the accepted CargoOffer at the offered→accepted
  transition and frozen for the rest of the Shipment lifecycle —
  reassignment is not supported in Phase 0/1 (cancel + re-quote instead).
  See erd-overview.puml for the cross-context wiring.
end note

@enduml
